Package: DistrViz
Type: Package
Title: Green Eyes, Flower Plots and Heatmaps for Distributional Data
Version: 1.0.0
Date: 2026-10-29
Authors@R: person(given = "Antonio", family = "Irpino", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "antonio.irpino@unicampania.it",
    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-9293-7180"))
Description: Graphical tools for distributional data tables, where each cell
    is a distribution: matrices of histograms ('HistDAWass' MatH objects),
    matrices of discrete distributions ('DDAWASS' MatD objects) or raw and
    tabulated discrete data. It draws Green Eyes plots, circular displays of
    all the distributions observed on a statistical unit, also placed on the
    factorial plane of a quantile-based principal component analysis (with an
    interactive version based on 'ggiraph'); difference eyes, showing where the
    quantile functions of a unit depart from the Wasserstein barycenter; flower
    plots, where each variable is a stem with petals as wide as the
    probabilities of its values; and distributional heatmaps, where each cell
    shows a whole distribution and rows and columns are ordered by
    Wasserstein-based hierarchical clustering. Variables can be ordered by the
    shortest Hamiltonian cycle on a correlation distance. Green Eyes plots
    were introduced in Crocetta, Irpino, Antonucci and Marin (2025)
    <doi:10.1007/s11135-024-01956-0>; the Wasserstein statistics follow Irpino
    and Verde (2015) <doi:10.1007/s11634-014-0176-4>.
